      "writtenOn": "2019-12-19T17:18:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The comment helps, but \"master\" still doesn\u0027t have much meaning here. Let\u0027s make the names more specific.\n\nI think the pd_enabled and try_src states have difference semantics.\n\nI would think that if master try_src was enabled, that would mean that try source mode was enabled. Not that it was enabled if other parts of the system also thought it should be enabled.\n\nAnd pd_enabled should be pd_disabled and it is a disable mask meaning multiple sources can disabled pd (e.g. protocol, security policy, etc.). Only if no one is disabling PD, do we allow PD. This is similar to the sleep mask.\n\nAlso when a pd_disabled flags is added, we should immediate reset the state machine to a disabled state (most likely through an event that the main loop processes) -- see below comment about infinite loop.\n\n\nTry source on the other hand probably is closer to a true override, meaning the \"master\" (either through console command or host command) overrides the current try source state regardless of what the state machine would normally set due to SoC state transitions.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 100,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 108,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "1c74476c4547e67a149ae87a5c729813b3c86329",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2d93a10b_042286b3",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_tc_drp_acc_trysrc_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 108,
      "author": {
        "id": 1149894
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-12-19T19:46:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Other than changing the name to PD_MASTER_ENABLE and TRY_SRC_MASTER_ENABLE, I can\u0027t seem to think of any other name that would make their function clearer. I\u0027m a little confused as to what you want me to do here. I\u0027m using the master enable to gate the setting of enable and I\u0027ve added a truth table to reflect this.\n\nAlso, when pd is disabled, all state machines except the type-c state machine are disabled. The disabled state is entered when the port is disabled, not just PD.",
      "parentUuid": "2be2a2b9_ee133de8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 100,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 108,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "1c74476c4547e67a149ae87a5c729813b3c86329",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "179ec7d5_20d78dc6",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_tc_drp_acc_trysrc_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 108,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-12-19T20:34:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Here are my suggestions:\n\n\n1) I am suggesting pd_enable becomes pd_disabled_mask.\nThen anyone checking the value will perform !pd_disabled_mask instead of pd_enable \u003d\u003d BIT(0) | BIT(1)\n\n2) For pd_disabled_mask, use names like CONNECTION_NOT_PRESENT BIT(0) and POLICY_PD_DISABLE BIT(1) as the flag names. bit0 might need a better name, but it represents the current use of pd_enable\n\n3) For try_src since the semantics are different, keep the existing variable just 0 and 1, and add a new variable that is try_src_override that has 3 values: NO_OVERRIDE, OVERRIDE_ON, and OVERRIDE_OFF\nThen try_src on logic is (override_try_src \u003d\u003d OVERRIDE_ON) || (override_try_src \u003d\u003d NO_OVERRIDE \u0026\u0026 try_src_enabled)\n\n(You could encode both try_src_enable and override_try_src in a single bit field var, but it doesn\u0027t seem like it is worth the overhead mixing a pure boolean field with a enum field within the same variable)\n\nThis will allow the override to always be able to set the try source state reguardless of what the power state of the SoC is, and also allow the SM to reset to what is \"should\" be after overriding is done.",
      "parentUuid": "2d93a10b_042286b3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 100,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 108,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "1c74476c4547e67a149ae87a5c729813b3c86329",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2c16e1ea_d359f6fb",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_tc_drp_acc_trysrc_sm.c",
